## 1.2.0

```
Gems tab - the settings window has a second tab for weapon gems. Every gem that deals damage gets a Damage setting, with its own General card (Multiply or At Least) that leaves your spells alone.
Gem stats - every gem's other numbers too: durations, cooldowns, tick intervals, chances, regeneration, armor, orb healing and more, for all 28 obtainable gems (with a Tier 7 row).
Gem summons - add levels to the Skull, Wretch and Reaper, or let them follow your own level with Sync With Player (experimental).
Gems - a gem takes its new values when its weapon is next equipped or switched to on the hotbar.
Values - the window shows what a multiplier gives next to it (for example "= 6 s"). Right-click a value to put it back to its default.
Shots Through Walls - new toggle for Totems, Lightning Wisp and Fire Wisp Scroll: their shots fly through terrain, walls and water and still hit enemies.
Ball Lightning - new Through Walls toggle: the ball flies through terrain, walls and water and still hits enemies.
F3 - now opens the settings window by default (was Shift+F3). If you already picked your own key in Kiln, you keep it.
Grimoire - with Grimoire 1.1.0 installed, F3 opens both windows side by side, and they move together while they touch. Hold Shift while dragging to move one alone. Needs Kiln 0.2.0-dev.31.11 or newer.
```

## 1.1.0

```
Cast Time - lowering it no longer makes spells fail to cast (Chain Lightning below x0.55, Lightning Wisp below x0.3, and other spells at lower values). Cast Time now only shortens how long you hold your staff before the spell goes off, down to x0.1 for every spell. The cast itself keeps its full length, so the spell always goes out.
Performance - changing a setting no longer freezes the game for a second or more. Only the values that actually change are rewritten, and quick changes in a row, like clicking a value several times, are applied together. Changing General Cast Time can still pause the game briefly.
Settings window - it can now be resized and moved, and it opens again where you left it, at the same size, even after restarting the game.
Perception - new setting for Totems, Skeleton, Lightning Wisp, Skull Vessel and Fire Wisp Scroll: how far the summon notices enemies and goes for them. Wisps' and totems' shots fly longer to match, so they still reach.
Shot Lifetime - new setting for Lightning Wisp and Fire Wisp Scroll, 5 s by default (the game's is 2 s). Their shots used to fade before reaching enemies at the edge of their range.
```

## 1.0.0

```
First release.
```
